cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use smaihda, please cite the S-MAIHDA preprint given under preferred-citation."
title: "smaihda: Simple-Means MAIHDA for binary outcomes in Stata, Python and R"
type: software
version: 1.9.0
date-released: 2026-10-06
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Lund-University-Social-Epidemiology/smaihda"
abstract: >-
  smaihda implements the simple-means form of the Multilevel Analysis of
  Individual Heterogeneity and Discriminatory Accuracy (MAIHDA) for binary
  outcomes, as a Stata command, a Python script and an R script that give the
  same point estimates. Version 1.9.0 is the version published with the
  S-MAIHDA preprint (version 2).
keywords:
  - MAIHDA
  - simple means
  - variance partition coefficient
  - discriminatory accuracy
  - health inequalities
